{
  "id": "participatory-action-research",
  "term": "participatory action research",
  "definition": "Participatory action research is a research approach used to develop and carry out actions or interventions with close attention to the real-world context in which they will be used. It is often combined with both qualitative and quantitative methods to improve understanding of contextual factors and support more realistic efforts to influence behaviour.",
